<body>
    <div class="page">
        <div class="header-logo">ABB</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 100px;">
            <div style="font-size: 12px; color: #555; margin-bottom: 5px;">APPLICATION NOTE AN001</div>
            <h1 style="font-size: 36px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;">Protection for Resistance Temperature Detectors (RTDs)</h1>
            <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">ESP AN001 for ESP 06D, ESP SL06, ESP 06Q, ESP RTD, ESP SL RTD, ESP RTDQ</h2>
        </div>
        <div style="height: 500px; background-image: url('placeholder_diagram_1.jpg'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;">
            <!-- Placeholder for the large diagram -->
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <span data-field="document_title_page_2">{{ document_title_page_2 }}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="content-block">
            <p>The Resistance Temperature Detector is a widely used device for measuring temperature. In basic terms, the electrical resistance of a sensing resistor, Rt, varies with temperature.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-block">
            <p>Temperature is simply measured indirectly by reading the voltage drop across the sensing resistor in the presence of a constant current flowing through it using Ohm's Law.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-block">
            <p>Fundamentally, every sensing resistor is a 2 wire device. It is essential that the resistance values of any external lead wires are taken into account.</p>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">2 Wire systems</h3>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>2 Wire systems offer poor accuracy due to lead resistance but are adequate for some industrial applications.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>This type of system can be protected using a single 2-channel ESP 06D or space saving Slim Line ESP SL06 surge protective device (SPD) (ESP 06D illustrated opposite).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-container">
            <!-- Diagram for 2 Wire systems -->
            <img src="placeholder_diagram_2_wire.png" alt="2 Wire System Diagram" style="max-width: 80%; height: auto;">
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">3 Wire systems - earthed bridge</h3>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>3 Wire systems allow for a good deal of lead resistance compensation and therefore offer better accuracy than a 2 wire system.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>In a typical 3 wire system, the bridge circuit is earthed as shown in the diagram opposite. It is therefore necessary to protect all three wires.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>This could be accomplished using two ESP 06D or ESP SL06 SPDs where only 1 channel of the second SPD is utilised. However, this would be bulky and not cost effective due to the unused channel.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-container">
            <!-- Diagram for 3 Wire systems - earthed bridge -->
            <img src="placeholder_diagram_3_wire_earthed.png" alt="3 Wire System Earthed Bridge Diagram" style="max-width: 80%; height: auto;">
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">3 Wire systems - floating bridge</h3>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>There are also 3 wire systems where the bridge circuit is not earthed and is said to be "floating".</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>In this system, a single ESP SL06 or ESP 06D SPD can be used to protect the 2 leads from the bridge arms whilst the third (supply) lead is connected to the SPD's earth via the screen connection (ESP 06D illustrated opposite).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-container">
            <!-- Diagram for 3 Wire systems - floating bridge -->
            <img src="placeholder_diagram_3_wire_floating.png" alt="3 Wire System Floating Bridge Diagram" style="max-width: 80%; height: auto;">
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <span data-field="document_title_page_3">{{ document_title_page_3 }}</span>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">4 Wire systems</h3>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>4 Wire systems provide the highest accuracy as the lead resistances and connection contact resistances have a negligible effect if the measuring circuit has high input impedance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>The leads are often connected to a constant current circuit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>All 4 channels can be protected using two ESP 06D or OVR SL06 SPDs (ESP SL06 illustrated opposite).</p>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Protecting multiple RTDs</h3>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>Where there are multiple RTD systems requiring protection, the ESP Q series variants, ESP 06Q and ESP RTDQ, can be utilised.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>The ESP 06Q provides protection for 4 pairs (8 channels) of wires whilst the ESP RTDQ will protect three sets of 3 wires (9 channels). Diagrams for each type are shown opposite.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
            <p>Thus space saving potential and cost effectiveness can be realised over the equivalent number of SPDs.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around; margin-top: 30px;">
            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <img src="placeholder_diagram_esp06q.png" alt="ESP 06Q Diagram" style="max-width: 45%; height: auto;">
                <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 10px;">An ESP 06Q unit is capable of protecting:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><span data-field="esp06q_feature_1">{{ esp06q_feature_1 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="esp06q_feature_2">{{ esp06q_feature_2 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="esp06q_feature_3">{{ esp06q_feature_3 }}</span></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <img src="placeholder_diagram_esprtdq.png" alt="ESP RTDQ Diagram" style="max-width: 45%; height: auto;">
                <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 10px;">An ESP RTDQ unit is designed to protect up to three 3 wire systems with an earthed bridge.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="table-container">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Part No.</th>
                        <th>ABB order code</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>ESP 06D</td>
                        <td><span data-field="part_no_esp06d_order_code">{{ part_no_esp06d_order_code }}</span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>ESP SL06</td>
                        <td><span data-field="part_no_espsl06_order_code">{{ part_no_espsl06_order_code }}</span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>ESP 06Q</td>
                        <td><span data-field="part_no_esp06q_order_code">{{ part_no_esp06q_order_code }}</span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
